      "side": 1,
      "message": "The same helper now has two different failure policies: in loadAddressBlocklist() an invalid entry returns EINVAL and fru-device exits, but here it logs and continues. Since the blocklist exists to keep fru-device from probing devices that can hang the bus, skipping a mistyped entry means that address is probed anyway.\n\nBefore this change an invalid entry here was inserted as a wrong address (e.g. \"11\" -\u003e 0), so this is not a regression, but is the log-and-skip intentional? If not, could this exit like the other blocklist validation errors in this function? Either way, please mention it in the commit message, since it says only, \"Valid single addresses behave as before\".",
      "revId": "a3219f18a462d07d61fbf035e743c135c618b6cf",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
